Runeglow

Runeglow is a Svelte 5 port of Libraries.dev by Jakub Antalik
(https://github.com/Jakubantalik/Libraries.dev), which is published under the
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Jakub Antalik.

The effect engines, stylesheet generators and shaders under
packages/runeglow/src/lib are carried over from that project, in most files
unchanged. The Svelte components that wrap them, and the site under apps/site,
are new.

The machine-learning models that Libraries.dev publishes (Magnet.mfxl and
VoicePosition.mfxl) are under a separate licence and are not part of this
project.

Third-party software

Liquid metal (packages/runeglow/src/lib/metal-fx) includes software developed
by Paper Design, Inc.

  Paper Shaders (https://github.com/paper-design/shaders)
  Copyright (c) Paper Design, Inc.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
  A copy is at packages/runeglow/LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

Specifically:

  * The `liquidMetal` fragment shader in
    src/lib/metal-fx/engine/liquidMetal.frag.ts is copied from the
    `@paper-design/shaders` npm package at version 0.0.80 by
    scripts/vendor-liquid-metal.mjs.

  * The sizing vertex shader in src/lib/metal-fx/engine/shaders.ts
    (`VERT_SHADER_SRC`) is copied from
    `packages/shaders/src/vertex-shader.ts` at 0.0.80, as it is in the
    upstream metal-fx package.

No changes were made to either shader's source.

Robot heads (packages/runeglow/src/lib/bot-avatars/robot) is a Svelte port of
software developed by Fayaz Ahmed.

  robot-heads (https://github.com/fayazara/robot-heads)
  Copyright (c) 2026 Fayaz Ahmed
  Licensed under the MIT License
  A copy is at packages/runeglow/LICENSES/robot-heads-MIT.txt.

Specifically:

  * geometry.ts, light.ts, faces.ts, sim.ts and render.ts are carried over
    from `src/tv` at version 0.3.0, and changed: two more shapes (capsule,
    octagon) and two more states (waiting, success); three shell finishes;
    round LEDs; the screen's light on its bezel and contact shading under
    the ears; meshes at three levels of detail; quads drawn grouped by
    colour; baked reliefs made at a few sizes and the least recently used
    dropped.

  * RobotHead.svelte, presets.ts and types.ts are new.
